# Markdown is excluded deliberately, and it is not a style opinion.
#
# Prettier's only disagreement with this repo's markdown is TABLE-CELL PADDING: it pads
# every cell to the column width, which turns the compact `|---|---|` tables that
# `architecture/` is built on into 400-character lines. Measured before adding the check:
# EVERY markdown file in the tree failed, including ones untouched for months.
#
# Formatting them would be a 40-file diff that makes the design documents harder to read,
# to satisfy a formatter that was never asked the right question. So the check is scoped
# instead — and scoped in the same commit that added it, because a required check that is
# red on day one for nobody's change is how a required check becomes non-required.
*.md

dist
node_modules
package-lock.json
public/landing

# Geometry fixtures are hand-laid-out coordinate lists that get READ and ported by humans —
# `architecture/v1/fixtures/README.md` treats them as a portable contract, and the strait
# test is the headline. Prettier explodes them: strait.fixture.json goes 40 → 82 lines for
# zero semantic change. Formatting data that is optimised for reading is a net loss.
**/*.fixture.json

# An annotated layout mockup, each region keyed to an ADR. Prettier takes it 379 → 1101
# lines and buries the annotations that are the whole point of the file.
architecture/v1/ux-wireframe.html
